target: internal/record/record.go
verify: go test ./internal/record/ -count=1 -run 'TestTheDecodeErrorNamesWhatTheOperatorMustGoFix'
expect: an over-long gate name must be truncated visibly
why:    a gate name is copied into the operator message verbatim, so one 1 MiB name produced a 1 MiB "message" — measured. The row cap in setErr bounds how many ROWS contribute and does not bound this, which is why removing this cap left the suite green.
--- old
		if len(name) > maxGateNameLen {
			name = name[:maxGateNameLen] + "..."
		}
--- new
		_ = maxGateNameLen
